{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c3d4e5f6-a7b8-9012-cdef-123456789012",
    "name": "FinRisk — seed smoke (3 requests)",
    "description": "Uses **stable IDs** from `db/seed/seed.sql` after a fresh seed:\n\n- **User 1** — first seed user (`u000001@seed.finrisk.local`).\n- **Account 1** — first Primary account; seed loads **three BUY** rows on assets **1–3** (`SEED00001` … `SEED00003`) so portfolio and risk are populated.\n\nSet **`baseUrl`**. No chained variables.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:18080" }],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 — Get seed user 1",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.code === 200);",
              "const u = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('seed email', () => u.email && u.email.includes('u000001'));",
              "pm.test('id is 1', () => u.id === 1);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/1"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "02 — Portfolio for account 1 (3 holdings from seed)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.code === 200);",
              "const p = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('three holdings', () => p.holdings && p.holdings.length === 3);",
              "const syms = p.holdings.map((h) => h.symbol).sort();",
              "pm.test('SEED00001–03', () => syms[0] === 'SEED00001' && syms[1] === 'SEED00002' && syms[2] === 'SEED00003');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/1/portfolio"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "03 — Risk for account 1 (volatility breakdown)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.code === 200);",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "console.log(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2));",
              "pm.test('three breakdown rows', () => j.breakdown && j.breakdown.length === 3);",
              "pm.test('score bounded', () => j.score >= 0 && j.score <= 100);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/1/risk"
      }
    }
  ]
}
